cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Simply Put in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Simply Put: a plain-language readability rig with a deterministic gate and a calibrated LLM judge"
abstract: >-
  Simply Put rewrites text to a target reading grade and gates the result
  with a deterministic, reproducible Flesch-Kincaid check. Meaning
  preservation, which cannot be computed that way, goes to a cross-vendor
  LLM judge calibrated against a human-human agreement ceiling on ASSET.
  The evaluation is multi-axis (faithfulness, omission, SARI, SLE) with
  negative controls on Med-EASi, using native Bumblebee metrics, an Oban
  batch runner, and a LiveView results dashboard.
type: software
